course: dictionary
lesson: 9778
title: What is a surname?
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A surname is your family name, the name you share with your family. In English names it usually comes last. In «Tom Smith», Smith is the surname.
explain: Schools use surnames a lot. Registers and class lists are often ordered by surname, and when you write to a teacher you might start with «Mr Jones» or «Mrs Patel», which both use the surname.
explain: Surnames often have a story. Many came from jobs (Smith, Baker), from places (Hill), or from a father's name: Johnson means John's son.
explain: Some names put the surname first. In «Wang Lei», Wang is the surname, because in Chinese names the family name comes first. If you are not sure which order someone wants, ask politely.
fact: A surname is your family name.
fact: «Surname» is a noun, and its plural is «surnames».
fact: The name Smith came from a job: a smith works with metal.
fact: Online, share only your first name with strangers, and never your full name and surname.
fact: With adults, start formal with «Mr», «Mrs», «Ms» or «Dr» and their surname, until they tell you to use their first name.
exercise: In «Tom Smith», which word is the surname? | Tom | Tom Smith | *Smith | Mr
exercise: Where do schools often use surnames? | In the school dinner queue | Only on football kits | In playground games | *In registers and class lists
exercise: In «Wang Lei», which word is the surname? | Lei | Wang Lei | *Wang | Xiǎo
test: What is a surname? | A pet's name | Your favourite colour | A number in a list | *Your family name
test: Which word is the surname in «Mrs Patel»? | Mr Patel | *Patel | Ms | Mrs
exam: Where did the surname Johnson come from? | A school subject | A king's castle | *A father's name, meaning John's son | A type of food
